<title>USA: US Ex-Im bank backs air reservation loan to Moscow.</title>
<headline>US Ex-Im bank backs air reservation loan to Moscow.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Export-Import Bank is financing a $118 million sale of a computer system to modernize the airline reservation systems of Russia and other nations of the former Soviet Union, the bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the bank would provide a $90 million loan guarantee to support the sales by International Business Machines Corp., AT&amp;T Corp. and SABRE Decision Technologies to the International Technological Corporation-Sirena of Moscow.</p>
<p>The bank said the reservation systems will enable Aeroflot and new private airlines in Russia and the newly independent states to provide services that match international standards.</p>
<p>It said that Vnesheconombank of Moscow is the borrower and Commerzbank AG of New York is the guaranteed lender.</p>
</text>
